    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d494">

                <pb facs="1201" n="1087" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg1087"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW/8–2243</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. J. Wesley Jones, of
                        the Division of European Affairs, to the Adviser on Political Relations</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Dunn</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-08-22">August 22, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>PA/D—<hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Dunn</hi> The attached message was left with
                    me yesterday by an officer of the O.S.S. It is
                    of interest as another “feeler” and channel from the Badoglio Govt.… the author
                    of the message is Dulles. I told the OSS to make
                    no reply to the question raised by the latter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">esley</hi>] J[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ones</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d494-a1.xml" xpointer="d494-a1"/>
            </div>
